{
  "slug": "mushroom-spinach-frittata",
  "name": "Mushroom and spinach frittata",
  "description": "Eggs baked with mushrooms, spinach and onion, finished with sharp cheddar cheese.",
  "iconKey": "crosshair",
  "instructions": [
    "Warm the olive oil in a 10-inch ovenproof skillet over medium heat and cook the onion until soft, about 3 minutes.",
    "Add the mushrooms and cook until browned and their liquid has evaporated, about 6 minutes.",
    "Stir in the spinach and cook just until wilted, then spread the filling evenly across the pan.",
    "Beat the eggs with the milk until smooth, pour them over the filling, and cook undisturbed until the edges set, about 8 minutes.",
    "Scatter the cheddar cheese over the top, slide the skillet under a hot broiler, and broil until the center is just firm, about 5 minutes."
